Re-deploying the same Maven coordinates with different content now replaces what
the repository serves. Previously the second upload was discarded while still
reporting success, so the repository went on serving the file deployed first,
which broke snapshot development silently: nothing indicated the new build had
not been stored. Artifacts are now distinguished by checksum as well as
coordinates, so re-uploading identical content remains a no-op and creates no new
repository version, while different content supersedes the previous file. The
artifact checksum is exposed on the content API.
